    "created_at": "2015-12-17T16:52:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-12-17T16:52:33Z",
    "body": "Thanks for working on this! A couple minor things:\n- Follow the guidelines in https://github.com/whatwg/html#pull-requests. In particular, wrap to 100 characters, and follow the guidelines for good commit messages. That means use present tense (\"Add\" instead of \"Added\") and use sentences for the second part (`Fixes #375.` instead of `Fixes \"#375\"`)\n- \"labeling\" is spelled with only two Ls, not three.\n- To better parallel the existing sentence structure, I'd suggest `for technical terms, taxonomic designation, transliteration, a thought, or for labeling ship names in Western texts, the <code>i</code> element should be used`.\n\nSorry to be nitpicky :). Just trying to guide you through these things so that future pull requests are seamless.\n",
